   "h": "Where",
   "text": "Tierras Altas is Panama's highland farm district on the slopes of **Volcán Barú**, beside **Parque Internacional La Amistad**, which Panama shares with Costa Rica. Its corregimientos are Volcán (the seat), Cerro Punta, Paso Ancho, Cuesta de Piedra and Nueva California, about 20,500 people in all (Census 2023, via IPM-C 2024). ✅ The landscape is cool, wet and steep: vegetable plots up the slopes, strawberries, flowers, dairy, and coffee lower down toward Boquete and Volcán. It is **not** the Panama of skyscrapers, the Canal or the Darién. That reaction is a fence; see 2b.",
