     "text": "**The reverse loan.** On Costa Rican coffee farms, part of pickers' pay was held back as a savings fund until the end of the harvest. In practice it worked as a guarantee for the farm owner and tied workers to the farm. Families who left early in Feb 2012 lost their share of the wages. Some farms held back money per *cajuela* to pay for the trip home.",
